WHATNOW

What tamlinux is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-26, with W43


STATE

  ROADMAP.md now defines the 17-milestone 0.7.x Northern Torch cultivar
  series across three phases: Phase 1 (bosgame bring-up and default
  switch, milestones 1-10), Phase 2 (replacing hyprlock/hypridle with
  tam-hide, replacing hyprsunset/hyprpicker with native tam-pane gamma
  and capture, porting laptop/display/input/window commands off hyprctl,
  and decoupling themes, menus, and Tensaku, milestones 11-14), and
  Phase 3 (deleting all Hyprland code, configs, adapters, hooks,
  patches, and tam-hyprland-* commands, removing the hypr*/aquamarine
  package tree and superseded dependencies across the fleet, and
  verifying sustained daily use on tam-pane alone, milestones 15-17)
  (W43).

  VERSION reads 0.7.1 on dev. The 0.7.1 desktop work is implemented in
  dev (W42). Both launch
  spellings, the benchmark, macro targeting, pointer focus, right-drag,
  and per-display tags passed focused checks. The new compositor pin
  is staged for the next candidate. Physical comparison awaits Test.

  The focus-border and lock change first pinned tam-pane 0.2.11 (W41).
  The packaged session sets a three-logical-pixel bright green focus
  border and routes manual Lock to tam-hide. The headless compositor
  and desktop suites pass. Physical focus and unlock await Test.

  Tamlinux 0.7.0 Northern Torch was prepared with
  tam-pane 0.2.10, tam-knox 1.1.2, tam 0.72.0 / 0.139.1, libtam 0.15.1,
  tam-clam 0.3.10, tam-data 1.0.3, tam-edit 1.2.0, tam-last 0.2.5,
  tamlinux-tools 0.1.2, tam-view 0.4.6, and tam-hide). Previous Run on
  bosgame is 0.6.42 (724b78a / 9e41c33). Meta + Return launches a new
  tam-last 0.2.4 window using tam-clam 0.3.5, preferring executable
  $HOME/.local/bin/tam-last and $HOME/.local/bin/tam-clam when present
  and falling back to /usr/bin/tamlinux/ (W29). Source installs pin both
  commands, and clipboard history paste targets the originating
  tam-last window. The current release is 0.5.12. Tamlinux 0.6 is the
  dependable Arch/Hyprland baseline.

